# SAVATE

Version 1.0

---

# Purpose

This document defines the physiological, biomechanical, technical and tactical demands of Savate Boxe Française.

Its purpose is to enable the Combat Athlete System (CAS) to understand the unique performance profile of Savate athletes and to individualize physical preparation accordingly.

This document describes performance requirements.

It does not prescribe training methods.

---

# Definition

Savate is a striking combat sport combining punches and highly technical kicks executed while wearing shoes.

Success depends upon:

Precision.

Timing.

Distance management.

Footwork.

Balance.

Technical efficiency.

Unlike many striking sports, accuracy and tactical intelligence often prevail over raw power.

---

# Philosophy

Savate is a sport of precision and movement.

Every strike should be technically efficient and tactically justified.

The athlete constantly alternates between attack, defense and repositioning.

Victory is often achieved through superior movement quality rather than overwhelming force.

